WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.509 --> 00:00:17.649
STUDENT: This is directed to you, Professor. Thank you for coming in.
I'd like to-- if you could

00:00:17.649 --> 00:00:18.289
just spend 

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:21.230
a bit more on your theory-- talking about secularization,

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.739
the aspect of the market--

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:28.899
and if you take Catholics out of the statistical analysis,
then it works, but if you put Catholics back in, it doesn't work.

00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:30.340
I was wondering why 

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.710
that is the case, why is it particularly

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.980
Catholics that sort of mess up

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.670
this economic model 

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:41.850
that's being proposed.
GORSKI: Well, right, I mean, the problem is double.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.820
First of all,

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.880
Catholic countries

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.920
do not have,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.190
typically, free markets and religion.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.150
And yet they tend to be--

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.560
this is the second point-- tend to be more observant

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.900
than Protestants do, at least if you look at contemporary
survey data.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.050
And this turned out to be true

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.609
on a smaller scale

00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:07.070
within the United States as well.  

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:13.600
In the US you also have the additional problem 
of Utah. In other words, Mormons, which don't

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.680
fit this model terribly well

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:22.360
either, and I think actually this anomaly 
is relatively easy to account for in terms of the kind of

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.090
organizational political model that I laid out,

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:30.740
which is-- number one, Catholics are the pioneers
in the development of missionary strategies,

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.190
particularly through the use of various
kinds of

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.390
preaching and teaching orders--

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.009
and this is one of the things which

00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:39.439
Protestantism

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:40.720
does away with,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.790
and doesn't really understand what it's lost.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.210
They have a much longer-standing

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:50.050
tradition of various kinds of parachurch organizations,
lay confraternities, sodalities,

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.610
other kinds of a quasi-religious organizations
like guilds

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:59.320
which then served as a kind of a platform
or a template during the nineteenth century for

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.900
the development of yet other forms

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.130
of lay--

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:06.600
lay association and parachurch organizations.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.490
And

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:11.019
you know, the one thing which of course
then becomes a problem

00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:12.739
for Catholics is that there

00:02:12.739 --> 00:02:14.749
tends to be this close

00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:15.429
relationship between--

00:02:15.429 --> 00:02:19.969
between church and state, and  so this is one--
this-- to the degree to which you observe

00:02:19.969 --> 00:02:21.629
secularization within 

00:02:21.629 --> 00:02:27.689
Catholic countries, it typically arises out
of this kind of political conflict between

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:28.930
kind of lay republicans

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:34.299
and increasingly kind of conventionalized
democratic mass parties.

00:02:34.299 --> 00:02:35.930
You know, France is

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.650
one-- is the best European example
of this, but, you know, Turkey in a way is kind of

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.789
you know-- I mean it's like,

00:02:42.789 --> 00:02:44.889
you know, it's like the most---

00:02:44.889 --> 00:02:47.260
it's an even more radical version 

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.019
of that same kind of process of secular, radical republicanism. 

